    <string name="dashboard_technical_glossary_title">Technical Glossary</string>
    <string name="dashboard_glossary_rsi_def">A score measuring if an asset moved too far, too fast. &gt;70 means Euphoria (high risk of a drop). &lt;30 means Panic (high probability of a bounce).</string>
    <string name="dashboard_glossary_macd_def">Shows the momentum of a trend. A Bullish crossover means buyers have taken control. A Bearish crossover means sellers are overwhelming the market.</string>
    <string name="dashboard_glossary_trend_def">The AI\'s objective evaluation of the current price action versus its historical moving averages, telling you who is currently winning the tug-of-war.</string>
    <string name="dashboard_glossary_sma_def">The average price over a set number of days. These act as invisible magnets. When price falls to a major SMA, institutional computers automatically buy to defend that level (Support).</string>

